# fib.bot -- naive recursive Fibonacci: calls, integer comparison and
# arithmetic.
#
# Canonical surface-Botlish source (CANONICAL-SURFACE-BENCHMARKS.md);
# migrated from the historical raw-core-IR fixture bench/fib.ir, which
# remains in bench/ only as a frozen input for historical audit-
# reproduction tooling (see that report) -- it is no longer canonical
# benchmark source. This is a direct, unremarkable transliteration: fib.ir
# never used any construct (like break VALUE) the surface language cannot
# express, so no workload/semantic decisions were needed here.
#
# expect: 17711

fn fib(n):
    if n < 2:
        n
    else:
        fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)

fib(22)
